From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: patrickjquinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 18:51:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] clk: Add MediaTek MT6358 clock buffer driver

Each output buffer of the MT6358 and MT6366 crystal oscillator is either
gated by hardware, following the SoC's clock requests, or switched by
software through an enable bit. Expose the buffers as clocks that a
consumer switches on by putting the buffer in software mode and setting
its enable bit.

Buffers under hardware control are reported as unprepared, and none of
the buffers is swept when unused, as the modem and the connectivity
subsystem use some of them without a Linux consumer.

The register layout is that of MediaTek's vendor clock buffer driver.

Signed-off-by: patrickjquinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
